## The fix

**`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:603-607`** (new clause in `scan-interpolation`, before the `=` debug-suffix check):

```clojure
(and (= phase :expr) (or (at j "<") (at j ">"))
     (= "=" (peek (inc j) 1)))
;; the comparisons <= and >= are one token: both chars at once, so
;; their trailing '=' never reaches the depth-0 debug-suffix check
(recur (+ j 2) depth (conj expr (peek j 2)) phase spec conv)
```

**Approach: option 1** — consume the two-character comparison tokens atomically. It extends the idiom the scanner already uses for `!=` (line 596) and `==` (line 604), and leaves the debug-suffix check itself byte-for-byte untouched. The clause appends the actual two chars (`peek j 2`), so the raw expression text is preserved exactly (`a <<= 1` still re-parses whole and refuses as the parser's own syntax error, matching CPython's statement-not-expression ruling).

## The pins

`test/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj:689-694`, in `fstring-golden-test`, following the existing golden shape — `f'{a <= 1}'` lowers to `py/le` over the global read of `a` and the literal `1`, wrapped in `py/format`; `f'{a >= 1}'` likewise with `py/ge` (the names from `comparison-ops`, lower.cljc:1520).

